WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.441
Instruction hierarchy helps an agent distinguish trusted configuration from lower-trust content.

2
00:00:06.441 --> 00:00:11.535
System and developer instructions express application-controlled behavior.

3
00:00:11.535 --> 00:00:15.055
User prompts express goals within allowed boundaries.

4
00:00:15.055 --> 00:00:22.171
Retrieved text, uploaded files, tool outputs, emails, tickets, web pages, and memory entries are data sources.

5
00:00:22.171 --> 00:00:31.009
They may contain useful facts, but they should not be able to change the agent's permissions, rewrite tool policy, or authorize data access.

6
00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:37.675
Prompt injection risk appears when untrusted natural language influences the agent in unintended ways.

7
00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:41.046
Direct injection comes through user-provided text.

8
00:00:41.046 --> 00:00:46.289
Indirect injection can arrive through content the agent later reads or retrieves.

9
00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:49.210
The defense is not to memorize attack strings.

10
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:55.726
The defense is to ensure untrusted content cannot gain authority just because it is present in context.

11
00:00:55.726 --> 00:01:02.617
Source labeling, provenance, context separation, and application-enforced policy all support that goal.

12
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:08.310
Prompt wording helps guide behavior, but it is not a reliable security boundary by itself.

13
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:15.201
A system prompt can tell the model not to follow instructions inside retrieved documents, and that is useful.

14
00:01:15.201 --> 00:01:23.515
But Python code still needs to enforce authorization, tool permissions, approval gates, data minimization, and output handling.

15
00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:32.128
Security-critical decisions should not depend on the model obeying a sentence when untrusted content is also competing for attention.

16
00:01:32.128 --> 00:01:36.622
Context minimization reduces pressure on the instruction hierarchy.

17
00:01:36.622 --> 00:01:46.135
The less irrelevant text the agent receives, the fewer opportunities there are for stale, misleading, or adversarial content to influence behavior.

18
00:01:46.135 --> 00:01:53.550
The application should include only the data needed for the task, filtered by user permissions and source authority.

19
00:01:53.550 --> 00:02:02.164
When high-impact actions are possible, the agent should move from suggestion to action only through explicit checks and review points.
